    (c) prompt construction, character identity conditioning, LoRA
        selection and trigger-word handling;
    (d) the WanGP client, model router, settings-manifest builder, and
        job queueing layer;
    (e) user interfaces, API routes, export and assembly tooling,
        configuration flows, and operational tooling; and
    (f) combinations of the foregoing.

For clarity, "Software" refers to the Licensor's implementation. It does
not, by itself, claim rights in abstract ideas, methods, concepts,
formats, protocols, or interfaces.

1.4 "Output" means any image, video, audio, text, metadata, file, or
other material generated by or through use of the Software.

1.5 "Headless Usage" means invoking or automating the Software without
using its web interface, including through scripts, batch runs, queue
processing, or command-line tooling.

1.6 "API" or "Integration" means any interface, wrapper, binding, SDK,
bridge, plugin, or service through which the Software is invoked.

1.7 "Direct Output Sale" means selling, licensing, or otherwise
charging separate consideration for an Output, or a collection of
Outputs, where the principal value of the transaction is the Output
